ok   the gzip decoder is installed by requiring cybertrain/http/gzip_ffi
ok   Accept-Encoding: gzip is sent and a gzip body is inflated under max_body
ok   a caller's Accept-Encoding is sent as written, not doubled
ok   a streamed gzip body yields inflated chunks
ok   get_to_file of a gzip body writes the inflated bytes
ok   an inflated body past max_body raises TooLargeError
ok   Content-Encoding: br is a BadResponseError
ok   corrupt or truncated gzip is a BadResponseError, buffered and streamed
ok   a gzip response with no body bytes is an empty body, kept and streamed
ok   an exception raised in the streamed block passes through the gzip sink unchanged
ok   HttpClient.gzip= replaces the gzip support
ok   a multi-member gzip body inflates to every member, buffered and streamed
ok   HEAD, 204 and a redirect's body are not inflated
ok   cleanup
